 ],
 "text": "How far away is a star? Henrietta Levitt found a clue in its blink. A faint star might be weak or just far away. She studied blinking stars in one distant cloud, all about equally far. They're the brighter ones blinked slower, so a blink gives true brightness and faintness then gives distance. Hubble later used her rule to show Andromeda is another galaxy. Lesson to see a real pattern compare like with like. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
